  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance to crisis-affected communities of Central African Republic - phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this new phase of emergency support to populations in CAR, this Consortium will work together to deliver essential activities designed to reduce the burden of like-threatening diseases and significantly reduce morbidity and mortality rates amongst the targeted populations. The Consortium will aim to achieve the specific objective of preventing and reducing excess morbidity and mortality of the population affected by the ongoing crisis in CAR. This will be achieved through strengthening of health facility and community capacity in terms of disease prevention and delivery of quality healthcare (including disease case  management, reproductive health, nutrition services, GBC, and WASH). Over 14 months, 14 health facilities (including 1 hospital) and a total of 85 CHWs and 25 FFPs will be supported across BK and OP prefectures.</narrative>
  </description>
